            "syn_cultural_context_a3a85a1a34f9"
          ],
          "text": "Genesis closes Jacob’s burial with an unresolved family fear. Joseph obtains Pharaoh’s permission to fulfill his oath to bury Jacob at Machpelah in Canaan, but after Jacob’s death his brothers fear that Joseph may now repay their earlier wrong. Joseph weeps, rejects their fear, and promises to provide for them and their children. His statement that they intended evil while God intended good identifies the preservation of many lives as the outcome he recognizes in their shared story.",
          "verse_refs": [
