          "id": "block_3",
          "interpretation_level": "disputed",
          "synthesis_ids": [
            "syn_interpretive_questions_8dc0e16d394a"
          ],
          "text": "The brothers report that Jacob commanded Joseph to forgive them, but Genesis has not previously narrated Jacob giving that instruction. The passage does not settle whether this was an unrecorded command or a message framed by brothers who remained afraid. What it does show clearly is their continuing anxiety after Jacob’s death and Joseph’s compassionate response.",
          "verse_refs": [
            "Genesis 50:16-17",
            "Genesis 50:24-26"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "kind": "interpretive_questions",
      "title": "A message from the brothers"
    },
