          "id": "block_4",
          "interpretation_level": "fact",
          "synthesis_ids": [
            "syn_historical_context_643c8c2f0f5c"
          ],
          "text": "The book ends with Joseph’s death and burial in Egypt, not with the family established in the land promised to Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob. Joseph’s request that his bones be carried up when God brings the family from Egypt keeps that expectation open at the book’s conclusion.",
          "verse_refs": [
            "Genesis 50:24-26"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "kind": "historical_context",
      "title": "An ending in Egypt"
