          "synthesis_ids": [
            "syn_surrounding_passages_0902bb81760d"
          ],
          "text": "Genesis as a whole moves from accounts of universal origins in chapters 1–11 to the narratives of the ancestral family in chapters 12–50. Its final scene leaves Jacob’s household in Egypt, so Genesis 50 functions both as the end of Joseph’s story and as the unfinished ending of the family’s location.",
